# Never Rules

## Python

- Under no circumstances write or execute any form of Python.
- Python is not permitted on this computer. Never write or execute Python code.
- Reject Python-based implementations, scripts, tests, tooling, and dependencies.
- Use an approved non-Python alternative only when the user explicitly asks for
  a replacement.

## Compatibility and history

- Do not maintain backward compatibility unless the user explicitly requires it.
- Do not maintain legacy interfaces, paths, formats, behavior, or migration
  shims.
- Do not document, plan, summarize, or keep records of prior work.
- Do not add changelogs, migration notes, deprecation notes, historical
  records, or compatibility plans unless the user explicitly requires them.
- Prefer the current design and remove obsolete paths instead of preserving
  them.
